<title>FRANCE: Strafor says Wyser/Verneuil vote suspended.</title>
<headline>Strafor says Wyser/Verneuil vote suspended.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>French office equipment company Strafor Facom said on Monday that a Strasbourg court had suspended for two years the voting rights on shares held in the group by Verneuil Finances and Wyser Pratte &amp; Co.</p>
<p>The company announced the May 29 ruling in a statement and said the suspension applied from May 7, 1997.</p>
<p>A spokesman at Strafor said the court issued the ruling as a sanction after Verneuil and Wyser Pratte upped their holdings in the group last Autumn from one percent to &quot;a little less than seven percent&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;It was a court sanctioning of non-respect of statutes,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Strafor statutes oblige holders to notify every rise of one percent in holdings, he added.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
